m","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Pension Fund Committee","time":"1.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Place and Resources Overview Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Place and Resources Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Family Hubs Programme Phase 1 received limited assurance, indicating control weaknesses in a new strategic initiative","lead":"New programmes with weak controls at launch create risk of budget overruns, poor delivery, or failure to achieve intended outcomes. Limited assurance in Phase 1 suggests Phase 2 implementation may face control challenges.","iso":"2026-08-03","paper_title":"Dorset Council Internal Audit Annual Opinion Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/documents/s53448/53448.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"20 audit actions are currently overdue, up from 9 in the prior year","lead":"Overdue audit actions indicate that management is not implementing agreed control improvements on schedule. Repeated action delays suggest weak accountability for remediation and increase the likelihood that identified gaps persist longer than documented.","iso":"2026-08-03","paper_title":"Dorset Council Internal Audit Annual Opinion Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/documents/s53448/53448.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"One Priority 1 Health and Safety action from prior-year investigation remains outstanding","lead":"Priority 1 actions outstanding for extended periods indicate the council is not acting urgently on serious identified risks. This suggests potential gaps in management accountability and the council's ability to remediate known compliance failures.","iso":"2026-08-03","paper_title":"Dorset Council Internal Audit Annual Opinion Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/documents/s53448/53448.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-08-03","committee":"Audit and Governance  Committee","paper_title":"Dorset Council Internal Audit Annual Opinion Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/documents/s53448/53448.pdf","headline":"Family Hubs Programme Phase 1 received limited assurance, indicating control weaknesses in a new strategic initiative","detail":"An audit of Family Hubs Programme Phase 1 found only limited assurance with 2 Priority 2 actions. This suggests the council is implementing a new programme without adequate controls over budget, delivery or governance. The report provides no detail on the nature of the programme or budget scale.","category":"governance","matters":"New programmes with weak controls at launch create risk of budget overruns, poor delivery, or failure to achieve intended outcomes. Limited assurance in Phase 1 suggests Phase 2 implementation may face control challenges.","figures":"2 Priority 2 actions; limited assurance opinion","quote":"Family Hubs Programme Phase 1 Final Limited 2 0 2 0 Medium","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-03","committee":"Audit and Governance  Committee","paper_title":"Dorset Council Internal Audit Annual Opinion Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/documents/s53448/53448.pdf","headline":"20 audit actions are currently overdue, up from 9 in the prior year","detail":"The council has 20 overdue audit actions as at 19 June 2026. Although the report notes this includes 10 Priority 3 actions now tracked (not included in prior years), the underlying trend shows persistent delays in implementing audit recommendations. The council remains at risk of actions slipping further past agreed closure dates.","category":"governance","matters":"Overdue audit actions indicate that management is not implementing agreed control improvements on schedule. Repeated action delays suggest weak accountability for remediation and increase the likelihood that identified gaps persist longer than documented.","figures":"20 overdue actions as at 19 June 2026; prior year 9 Priority 1/2 overdue actions","quote":"Whilst the charts above show an increase in overdue actions (increasing from 9 to 20), this also includes 10 Priority 3 actions that would not have been included in last year's review.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-03","committee":"Audit and Governance  Committee","paper_title":"Dorset Council Internal Audit Annual Opinion Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/documents/s53448/53448.pdf","headline":"One Priority 1 Health and Safety action from prior-year investigation remains outstanding","detail":"A 2024/25 investigation into health and safety compliance resulted in 35 actions. As of the follow-up in 2025/26, three actions remain unresolved, including one Priority 1 (major concern requiring immediate corrective action). This action has been outstanding for at least 6 months since the action plan was issued in December 2025.","category":"audit","matters":"Priority 1 actions outstanding for extended periods indicate the council is not acting urgently on serious identified risks. This suggests potential gaps in management accountability and the council's ability to remediate known compliance failures.","figures":"1 Priority 1 outstanding; 3 total outstanding from 35 actions; action plan issued December 2025","quote":"of the 35 actions identified from the investigation, only 3 are outstanding (one Priority-1 and two Priority-2).","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-03","committee":"Audit and Governance  Committee","paper_title":"Dorset Council Internal Audit Annual Opinion Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/documents/s53448/53448.pdf","headline":"Governance of financial management in schools received limited assurance","detail":"Schools' financial management systems were audited and found to have limited control effectiveness, with 5 actions agreed (4 Priority 2, 1 Priority 3). As the council is statutorily responsible for schools' financial oversight, weak school finance controls represent a gap in the council's overall control environment.","category":"governance","matters":"The council is accountable for schools' finances. Weak school-level financial controls increase risk of misappropriation, budget overruns or reporting errors that affect the council's consolidated position and reputation.","figures":"5 actions (4 Priority 2, 1 Priority 3); limited assurance opinion issued","quote":"Governance of Financial Management in Schools Final Limited 5 0 4 1","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-03","committee":"Audit and Governance  Committee","paper_title":"Dorset Council Internal Audit Annual Opinion Report","paper_url":"https://moderngov.dorsetcouncil.gov.uk/documents/s53448/53448.pdf","headline":"Data Maturity controls received limited assurance, creating potential reliability risk for financial decisions","detail":"An audit of data maturity governance found only limited assurance, with 10 Priority 2 actions identified. The council's data systems and governance practices are weak enough that they may not reliably support financial and strategic decision-making. The report notes that actions require time to be embedded.","category":"governance","matters":"A council's financial position and forecasts depend on reliable data. If the council's data governance is immature, there is material risk that financial reporting, reserves forecasting, and budget monitoring are less reliable than they appear.","figures":"10 Priority 2 actions identified for data maturity","quote":"During 2025/26, three limited assurance opinions have been reported to the Committee relating to Data Maturity, Governance of Financial Management in Schools and Family Hubs Programme Phase 1","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-08-03"},"name":"Dorset UA","findings_total":51,"news_drafts_total":3}}